            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "fw-update/device_updater.cpp",
                    "line": 60,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "I am against adding logs like these in pldm code base. If we need more readable logs, please feel free to add fw_update spec support to pldm dissector in Wireshark.\n\nIBM took a lot of effort in getting the base & platform spec supported in pldm wireshark dissecter. Dont want the code base to be polluted with these logs in yet another verbose option."
                },
                {
                    "file": "fw-update/device_updater.cpp",
                    "line": 60,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P Arun Kumar Reddy",
                        "email": "arunpapannagari23@gmail.com",
                        "username": "arun-reddy23"
                    },
                    "message": "From what I could see online Wireshark helps analyze the network traffic, but in the case of FW Update using large bundles (>140M) the packets captured would make it hard to debug any FW Update failures for specific components. These logs would help speed up the debug process"
                },
                {
                    "file": "fw-update/device_updater.cpp",
                    "line": 60,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tom Joseph",
                        "email": "rushtotom@gmail.com",
                        "username": "tomjoseph83"
                    },
                    "message": "The bulk of PLDM T5 traffic is the Tx/Rx of RequestFirmwareData where PLDM FD downloads image from the BMC. With the number of PLDM devices we support on a platform, the total amount of data we transfer exceeds 140+ M, capturing MCTP traffic for this and adding it to BMC dump is not a feasible solution. \n\nSo printing Tx/Rx for the RequestFirmwareData without the actual data firmware data, gives decent debug capabilities on the BMC when PLDM firmware update is in progress and helped us triage issues where logs on the device has been insufficient.\n\nI agree with Manoj's concern in principle, there are platform specific needs where such flexibility is needed. Also unlike a feature flag where more forethought is needed, flag for debug tracing has minimal side effects."
                },
                {
                    "file": "fw-update/device_updater.cpp",
                    "line": 60,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "> From what I could see online Wireshark helps analyze the network traffic, but in the case of FW Update using large bundles (>140M) the packets captured would make it hard to debug any FW Update failures for specific components. These logs would help speed up the debug process\n\nWireshark has the capability to dissect as big as 1G packet captures. It even has capabilities to split packet captures into multiple parts before it can be dissected using standard tools like `editcap`.\n\n\n> capturing MCTP traffic for this and adding it to BMC dump is not a feasible solution.\n\nIf this needs to be captured as part of the BMC dump, can we not just add them as `INFO` messages written into the journal, rather than a new verbose option which under the cover puts things into the journal ? I still think we are complicating this more than it needs to be by putting this behind yet another verbose option."
                },
                {
                    "file": "fw-update/device_updater.cpp",
                    "line": 60,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I also disagree with adding such logs. I agree that a pcap/Wireshark is a much more concise approach. You don't have to capture all traffic on an interface, you can be selective. See e.g. [tcpdump](https://www.tcpdump.org/manpages/tcpdump.1.html)'s filter expressions and [pcap-filter](https://www.tcpdump.org/manpages/pcap-filter.7.html). There might be some work required to make filter expressions more ergonomic for MCTP, but in the worst case you have the `byte` directive..."
                }
            ],
